---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import smallSparse from '../../generated/small-sparse.json';
import registry from '../../generated/registry.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

interface SchoolRow {
  school: string;
  name: string;
  supervisory_union: string | null;
  grade_span_class: string | null;
  grades_as_stated: string | null;
  municipality: string | null;
  municipality_basis: string;
  land_area_sq_mi: number | null;
  population: number | null;
  density: number | null;
  enrollment: number | null;
  small_screen_met: boolean | null;
  sparse_screen_met: boolean | null;
  enrollment_status: string;
  density_status: string;
  determination_status: string;
}

const data = smallSparse as unknown as {
  generated: string;
  parameter_set_ref: string;
  fiscal_year: number;
  nothing_is_computable: boolean;
  why: string[];
  counts: Record<string, number>;
  population_series_held: string[];
  schools: SchoolRow[];
};

const names = new Map(
  (registry.entities as Array<{ slug: string; name: string }>).map((e) => [e.slug, e.name]),
);

// Public schools only in the table. Independents and tech centres are in the
// registry because they are receiving schools in consolidation scenarios, but
// they are not candidates for these grants and listing them here would imply
// they were.
const rows = data.schools
  .filter((r) => r.municipality !== null)
  .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));

const withoutTown = data.counts['schools'] - data.counts['with_municipality'];
---

<Base
  title="Small and sparse schools — Vermont School Budgets"
  description="The two statutory screens for the Act 73 small and sparse school support grants, and why no school in Vermont can yet be screened against them."
>
  <h1>Small and sparse schools</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Act 73 of 2025 creates support grants for schools that are small or sparse
    <em>by necessity</em>. This page holds the geography those grants turn on. It holds no
    verdicts, and it will not until somebody reads the enacted acts — the reason is below,
    stated before the table rather than after it.
  </p>

  <div class="notice blocking">
    <strong>Nothing on this page says whether a school qualifies.</strong>
    <p>
      Three separate things stand between this table and an answer, and they belong to three
      different parties:
    </p>
    <ul>
      {data.why.map((reason) => <li>{reason}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>
      The middle one is ours. The first is ours too. The third is the State's, and it is not a
      criticism: the Agency of Education cannot publish determinations under rules that do not
      exist yet.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What the statute asks</h2>
  <p>
    Two screens, both arithmetic. A school is <strong>small</strong> if its enrollment is below
    a threshold. A school is <strong>sparse</strong> if the municipality it stands in has fewer
    than some number of people per square mile <em>of land</em>. Both thresholds are in
    <a href={`${base}/methodology/small-sparse/`}>the parameter file</a>, and both are null.
  </p>
  <p>
    Meeting both screens does not make a school eligible. Eligibility additionally requires a
    determination of <em>necessity</em> — that the school is small or sparse because of
    geography or isolation rather than because of a local decision. Nobody has made that
    determination for any school in Vermont, and the criteria for making it are a proposal to
    the State Board rather than a rule.
  </p>
  <p>
    One of the proposed criteria matters for how this page should be read: a school is not
    disqualified by being <em>above</em> the enrollment threshold today, because the framework
    contemplates places whose enrollment dips temporarily. The enrollment screen is a candidate
    filter, not a gate.
  </p>

  <h2>What is here, and what is not</h2>
  <table class="scroll-x">
    <caption>Coverage of the inputs the two screens need</caption>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Schools in the registry</th>
        <td>{data.counts['schools']}</td>
        <td>Every open school, academy and technical centre.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Located in a municipality</th>
        <td>{data.counts['with_municipality']}</td>
        <td>
          Resolved from AOE-published coordinates against Census county subdivisions, not from
          the mailing address. A Vermont post office name routinely covers parts of several
          towns.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">With land area</th>
        <td>{data.counts['with_land_area']}</td>
        <td>Census Gazetteer ALAND. Land only — total area would understate density.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">With municipal population</th>
        <td>{data.counts['with_population']}</td>
        <td>
          {data.population_series_held.length === 0
            ? 'None retrieved: the Census data API requires a key for county-subdivision queries and this build had none.'
            : `Series held: ${data.population_series_held.join(', ')}.`}
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">With school-level enrollment</th>
        <td>{data.counts['with_enrollment']}</td>
        <td>
          AOE publishes average daily membership by <em>resident district</em>, which is a town
          rather than a school. No per-school series is available through the public API, and a
          town's membership standing in for a school's roll would be a fabrication that looked
          like data.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Screens resolved</th>
        <td>{data.counts['screens_resolved']}</td>
        <td>
          Zero, and it stays zero while the thresholds are unverified — independently of every
          row above.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  {withoutTown > 0 && (
    <p class="note">
      {withoutTown} schools are not in the table because their municipality is not established:
      AOE publishes no coordinates for them, or their coordinates fall in a place the registry
      tracks only through an incorporated school district. Both cases are listed in
      <code>derived/school-municipality/</code> rather than quietly dropped.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>The candidate geography</h2>
  <p class="note">
    Population and enrollment columns are blank for the reasons above. The density column is
    what it will be computed from, once there is a population series and a verified threshold to
    compare it against.
  </p>

  <table class="scroll-x">
    <caption>
      {rows.length} schools with an established municipality. FY{data.fiscal_year} frame,
      computed against <code>{data.parameter_set_ref}</code>.
    </caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">School</th>
        <th scope="col">Town</th>
        <th scope="col">Grades</th>
        <th scope="col">Land area (sq mi)</th>
        <th scope="col">Population</th>
        <th scope="col">Density</th>
        <th scope="col">Small screen</th>
        <th scope="col">Sparse screen</th>
        <th scope="col">Necessity</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {rows.map((row) => (
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">{row.name}</th>
          <td>{row.municipality ? names.get(row.municipality) ?? row.municipality : '—'}</td>
          <td>{row.grades_as_stated ?? '—'}</td>
          <td>{row.land_area_sq_mi?.toFixed(1) ?? '—'}</td>
          <td>{row.population ?? '—'}</td>
          <td>{row.density?.toFixed(1) ?? '—'}</td>
          <td><span class="tag unverified">{row.enrollment_status.replace(/_/g, ' ')}</span></td>
          <td><span class="tag unverified">{row.density_status.replace(/_/g, ' ')}</span></td>
          <td><span class="tag undetermined">{row.determination_status}</span></td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Reading the blanks</h2>
  <p>
    Four kinds, and the site never renders two of them the same way. See
    <a href={`${base}/methodology/#blanks`}>the methodology page</a> for the full legend.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <span class="tag unverified">unverified</span> — a statutory value has not been checked
      against current law. <strong>Ours.</strong>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="tag missing-input">missing input</span> — the source document does not
      publish it. <strong>A fact about the document.</strong>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="tag undetermined">undetermined</span> — the State has not made a decision
      that does not yet exist. <strong>Nobody's, yet.</strong>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="tag not-computable">not computable</span> — the question cannot be answered
      from public data at all. <strong>Nobody's, ever.</strong> Four of the five necessity
      criteria are permanently in this category, and that is a correct answer rather than an
      outstanding task.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="note">
    Generated {new Date(data.generated).toISOString().slice(0, 10)}.
  </p>
</Base>
